EXT. HOSPITAL ROOFTOP HELIPAD - NIGHT

Wind pulls at orange windsocks. Rotor noise rises. A helicopter settles on the pad in a storm of grit.

DR. NASRIN FAROUQ, 40s, scrubs under a puffer jacket, crouches low beside a gurney. BEA OYELARAN, 30s, charge nurse, grips the rail. Both squint into the downwash.

Doors slide open. TOMMASO RINALDI, 30s, flight medic, jumps out with a monitor in his arms, shouting over the blades.

TOMMASO
Male, thirties, fall from scaffold. Two stories. BP seventy over forty, GCS ten.

NASRIN
Any ID?

TOMMASO
Nothing on him. Nobody came with him.

They lift the patient out. A YOUNG MAN, 30s, pale, dust in his beard, eyes half-open, strapped to the board. Bea runs beside the gurney.

BEA
Sir. Sir, can you hear me?

The young man's lips move. Bea leans down.

YOUNG MAN
(faint)
Where's my boy.

BEA
Who's your boy?

YOUNG MAN
Waiting. At the site gate.

NASRIN
What's your name, sir?

YOUNG MAN
Desmond. Desmond Achebe.

INT. HOSPITAL ELEVATOR - CONTINUOUS

Doors close. The gurney fills the car. Tommaso holds a bag valve mask. The elevator hums downward.

NASRIN
Desmond, I'm Dr. Farouq. You're in a hospital. We're taking you straight to trauma.

DESMOND
My son's six. He'll think I left him.

BEA
Then we'll find him, Desmond. I'll call the site foreman myself.

TOMMASO
(low)
Doc, pressure's dropping.

NASRIN
Bea, two units O-neg, wide open. Tommaso, stay on his airway.

The elevator dings. Doors open onto the bright, loud corridor of the emergency department.

NASRIN (CONT'D)
Stay with me, Desmond. Talk to Bea about your son.

Bea walks fast beside the bed.

BEA
What's his name?

DESMOND
Kwabena. Kwabena likes dinosaurs.

BEA
Then Kwabena is going to meet the biggest dinosaur in this building. You hold on.

They roll out of frame.
